R87-A head-latency probe instrument (PR #469) — extracted from the scored surface.

Applies against: 3217f111142346e004f41fae611a8bede172a659
  (the fork point of maple-tanjiro/r87-routed-qmv-head-latency; it predates
   PR #456, which moved 2,591 lines of LagunaRuntimeModel.swift into
   Sources/MLXFastModel/LagunaRuntimeLayers.swift. Against any base at or after
   #456 the routed gate/up generator lives in LagunaRuntimeLayers.swift, so the
   hunks need `git apply -3` or manual placement.)

Re-apply:
  git checkout -b <branch> 3217f111142346e004f41fae611a8bede172a659
  git apply research/tanjiro_r87a_probes.patch

Why this is a patch and not code: the R87-A hypothesis was refuted. Every
submittable arm regressed the touched kernel by +26 to +106 µs/step against a
per-kernel σ of 3.51, so all three knobs are dead code on a dead hypothesis,
and one of them is deliberately numerically incorrect.

  DARKBLOOM_ROUTED_GATEUP_INPUT_PF  0..3, default 0. Input-vector preload for
      laguna_routed_nvfp4_swiglu_qmv_packed_top8keys_r1_bf16_v2. 1 = steady
      state (stage the next block's input_values in the k-loop), 2 = preamble
      (hoist block 0 above the routing prelude), 3 = both. Bit-exact by
      construction; the default was verified byte-identical MSL to stock.
  DARKBLOOM_PROBE_ROUTED_GATEUP_BARRIERS  0..16, default 0. Injects N extra
      threadgroup_barrier(mem_flags::mem_none) per k-loop iteration. This is
      the positive control behind the standing finding that an in-kernel
      barrier costs 0.0293 µs per barrier per dispatch, ~48x below rule 41's
      per-dispatch-boundary cost.
  DARKBLOOM_PROBE_ROUTED_EXPERT0_PF  default off. DELIBERATELY INCORRECT: it
      hardcodes expert = 0 for the block-0 weight and scale addresses so the
      router->address dependency can be priced. Never submittable. It also
      collapses block-0 weight bytes ~8:1, so its −83.64 µs/step is a loose
      upper bound on the head-latency family, not a target.

Also included, and reusable on its own merits if a live mechanism ever needs
it: the source-generator refactor that turns the inline
`private let lagunaRoutedSwiGLUQMVPackedTop8R1Kernel` string literal into
`lagunaRoutedGateUpR1KernelName` + `lagunaRoutedGateUpR1Source()` with
interpolation, including the rule-33 kernel-name suffixing that stops the
pipeline cache from poisoning an A/B. Do not redo it from scratch.

